# babycc

A teaching-scale rewrite of the Claude Code agent loop, running against
gemma4:26b served by Ollama on vms.local. Stdlib only, about 300 lines.

## Run

```bash
cd ~/Code_2026/babycc
uv run babycc            # new session in the current directory
uv run babycc -c         # resume the latest session for this directory
uv run babycc --yolo     # skip bash approval prompts
```

The SSH tunnel to vms.local opens automatically if Ollama is not already
reachable on 127.0.0.1:11434. It authenticates as the dedicated
`ollama-tunnel` user, which vms.local's sshd restricts to forwarding that
one port.

## How it works

```
REPL -> send history + tools to gemma4 via Ollama
     -> model wants tools? execute, append results, send again
     -> model answered in text? print it, back to the REPL
```

Four tools: `bash` (with y/n approval), `read_file`, `write_file`,
`edit_file`. History is append-only, so Ollama's KV prefix cache makes
every turn after the first one fast.

Sessions persist to `~/.babycc/sessions/<cwd-slug>/` after every turn.

## Layout

| File | Role |
|---|---|
| `src/babycc/main.py` | REPL, agent loop, permission gate |
| `src/babycc/tools.py` | tool schemas and executors |
| `src/babycc/session.py` | conversation persistence |
| `src/babycc/tunnel.py` | SSH tunnel to vms.local |

## Test

```bash
uv run pytest            # unit tests, no LLM needed
./scripts/smoke.sh       # live end-to-end test against gemma4:26b
```

## Benchmark local models

Run one pass of the fixed babycc tool-loop task suite against both local
Gemma tags:

```bash
uv run python scripts/bench_models.py
```

Run a more stable comparison with repeated trials:

```bash
uv run python scripts/bench_models.py --repetitions 3
```

For a fast one-model check:

```bash
uv run python scripts/bench_models.py \
  --models gemma4:26b-mlx \
  --repetitions 1 \
  --tasks read_file,bash
```

For cold-start measurements, unload the model before each run:

```bash
uv run python scripts/bench_models.py --cold --repetitions 1
```

The wrapper writes:

- `reports/bench-*/metadata.json` with git and Ollama state
- `reports/bench-*/results.jsonl` with per-run pass/fail, timing, tools, and transcript path
- `reports/bench-*/transcripts/*.txt` with raw babycc output
- `reports/bench-*/summary.md` with a compact table

## Probe Ollama request shapes

Before debugging the agent loop, probe the model directly through Ollama:

```bash
uv run python scripts/probe_ollama.py --model gemma4:26b --timeout 90
```

Run selected cases when isolating a failure:

```bash
uv run python scripts/probe_ollama.py \
  --model gemma4:26b \
  --cases plain_think_false,babycc_tools_small_ctx \
  --timeout 90 \
  --cold
```

The probe records raw `/api/chat` responses under `reports/probe-*`.
It is useful for comparing plain chat, streaming, tool calls, thinking mode,
and smaller context settings without involving babycc's tool executor.

See `docs/agentic-investigation-plan.md` for the staged model reliability plan.

## Run small agent tasks

After the toy tool-loop benchmark passes, run the first real-task tier:

```bash
uv run python scripts/agent_tasks.py --models gemma4:26b
```

The initial task set creates disposable fixture repos and checks:

- repo survey into a written architecture summary
- single-file bug fix against `unittest`
- multi-file feature plus test update
- command failure recovery
- saved-session resume behavior

For a repeated baseline:

```bash
uv run python scripts/agent_tasks.py --models gemma4:26b --repetitions 3
```

The wrapper writes raw transcripts, validation output, and a summary under
`reports/agent-*`.

## Run high-school math tasks

To test model-only high-school math without babycc tools:

```bash
uv run python scripts/math_tasks.py --models gemma4:26b,gemma4:26b-mlx
```

The suite covers algebra, functions, geometry, probability, statistics,
trigonometry, logarithms, exponents, inequalities, and polynomials. It asks for
final answers only and grades exact answers with simple normalization for
fractions and `pi`.

For repeated deterministic runs:

```bash
uv run python scripts/math_tasks.py \
  --models gemma4:26b,gemma4:26b-mlx \
  --repetitions 3 \
  --temperature 0 \
  --think false
```

For slower reasoning-mode math runs, especially with the MLX tag:

```bash
uv run python scripts/math_tasks.py \
  --models gemma4:26b-mlx \
  --temperature 0 \
  --think true \
  --num-predict 1024
```

The wrapper writes raw Ollama responses and a summary under `reports/math-*`.

## Configuration

| Env var | Default | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `BABYCC_MODEL` | `gemma4:26b` | any Ollama model with tool support |
| `BABYCC_KEEP_ALIVE` | `1h` | Ollama keep-alive duration for the loaded model |
| `BABYCC_THINK` | unset | set to `false` or `true` to force Ollama thinking mode |
| `BABYCC_NUM_CTX` | unset | set Ollama `options.num_ctx` for the request |
| `BABYCC_NUM_PREDICT` | `1024` | set Ollama `options.num_predict` for the request |

## Design

See `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-03-babycc-design.md`.


